=== 2026-09-03 env change #2 (FINAL / persistent) ===
BEFORE: user env OLLAMA_FLASH_ATTENTION=1, OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0
ACTION: [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable('OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE','q4_0','User')
        killed all ollama processes by PID, relaunched "ollama app.exe" from a shell with
        $env:OLLAMA_FLASH_ATTENTION=1 and $env:OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q4_0.
        (The app inherits its parent's env; launching it without those set gave
         FLASH_ATTENTION:false / KV_CACHE_TYPE:"" and the model thrashed. On a normal
         logon it reads the user env vars from the registry, which now say q4_0.)
AFTER:  server.log confirms OLLAMA_FLASH_ATTENTION:true OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE:q4_0
WHY KEPT: q4_0 halves KV (this model caches only 16 of 66 layers), which is exactly the
        headroom that lets num_gpu 66 fit. Enables 64k on Q3_K_S/IQ3_M and 2.3x tok/s on
        Q3_K_M. No measured speed cost anywhere. Quality cost of q4_0 KV NOT measured.
REVERT: SetEnvironmentVariable('OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE','q8_0','User'); restart Ollama app.
        Also drop q27-IQ3_M-64k / q27-Q3_K_S-64k to num_ctx 32768, as they need q4_0 to fit.

FINAL STATE: desktop Ollama app running (as found), q4_0 + flash attention on.
  VRAM 394 MiB idle, 0 models loaded, ollama RSS 114 MB, disk 68 GB free.
  Independent watchdog (results/gpu-watch.log, another session's) recorded no ALERT;
  min free host RAM across the whole session 27.8 GB.

